import Causal.GXSingularDEC25
import Causal.Remarks.MassiveManifold
import Causal.Port.E0Axioms
import Causal.Port.E0SingularFlat

/-!
# `E^{1,2}_{≥0}`-manifolds over DEC-25 atlases: arc-connected, push-up, one natural causality

Target `T-ett-massa-dec25` (2026-11-21), split from `T-ett-singular-instance`. Cited, **unmarked**
(SCOPE): `cor:massA_causalite` — `ETT.tex:1396`, `cor:massA_cac` — `ETT.tex:1408`,
`cor:pushup_sing` — `ETT.tex:1419`. The three corollaries of `Causal.Remarks.MassiveManifold`,
restated over gx's almost-everywhere atlases (DEC-25, `Causal.GXSingularDEC25`) in place of the
abstracted atlas of `Causal.GXSingular`. What is proved needs neither `hreg` (the second half of (b)
of `prop:GX_sing_espace_temps_topo`) nor (b′) (OQ-64): `cor:massA_cac`, `cor:pushup_sing` and the
uniqueness half of `cor:massA_causalite`. The existence half is stated with `hreg`, (b′) named.

> Every $\mass{\geq 0}$-manifold carries a natural absolutely minimal causality. [Proof:] By
> Corollary \ref{cor:model_minimal} the model spaces $\mass{\kappa}$, $\kappa\geq0$, are
> absolutely minimal, and $\isom(\mass{})$ acts on $\mass{}$ by morphisms of topological
> spacetimes; $\mass{}$ is moreover locally compact Hausdorff, hence Baire. The hypotheses of
> Proposition \ref{prop:GX_sing_espace_temps_topo} are therefore satisfied by the analytic
> singular structure $(\isom(\mass{}),\mass{},\mass{\geq0})$, which yields the causality; it is
> absolutely minimal by Theorem \ref{theo:causalite_engendre}. (`ETT.tex:1396–1406`)

> Every $\mass{\geq 0}$-manifold is causally arc-connected. [Proof:] The chart domains form a cover
> of $M$ by causally arc-connected open sets: the model spaces are causally arc-connected, hence so
> are their open subsets by Remark \ref{rem:cac_local}. In particular $M$ is locally causally
> arc-connected, and by Proposition \ref{prop:GX_sing_espace_temps_topo} its causality is the one
> generated by that cover. [...] (`ETT.tex:1408–1417`)

> Every $\mass{\geq0}$-manifold has the push-up property. [Proof:] The chart domains form a cover
> of $M$ by open sets isomorphic, as topological spacetimes, to open subsets of the model spaces
> (Corollary \ref{cor:massA_causalite}); each of them has the push-up property by Remark
> \ref{rem:pushup}. Moreover $M$ is causally arc-connected by Corollary \ref{cor:massA_cac}. Lemma
> \ref{lem:pushup_local} concludes. (`ETT.tex:1419–1428`)

## What is proved (no `sorry` in this file)

* `IsAtlasCausalityDEC25 G C DX DY`, the natural causality over the DEC-25 atlas: every chart of
  the maximal a.e. atlas an isomorphism onto `X`, every `X_A`-chart (`IsAEChart` into a model) one
  onto its model, absolutely minimal. `IsoChartsCoverDEC25`: some chart at each point is an
  isomorphism. Bridge: `isAtlasCausalityDEC25_iff` — it is `IsAtlasCausality` for `I` the charts
  of the maximal a.e. atlas and `J` the `X_A`-charts.
* `cor:massA_cac`: `massA_cac_dec25`, local form `massA_cac_dec25_of_isoChartsCover`.
  `cor:pushup_sing`: `pushup_sing_dec25`, `pushup_sing_dec25_of_isoChartsCover`.
* `cor:massA_causalite`, uniqueness: `massA_causalite_unique_dec25` (an absolutely minimal
  causality with an isomorphic chart at each point is the natural one), **no hypothesis on the
  models**; `IsAtlasCausalityDEC25.eq`. Existence: `massA_causalite_dec25` (`hreg`, (b′) named),
  and given `hreg` it is exactly (b′): `forall_exists_isAtlasCausalityDEC25_iff`; assembled:
  `massA_singular_dec25`.
* The models of `E_{≥0}`: `MassAModel` (`E₀` at `none`, `E_κ` at `some κ`), `massAModelCausality`,
  `massAModel_facts` (each causally arc-connected and push-up, `E₀` included). With their singular
  structures abstract: `massA_dec25_models_of_isoChartsCover`, `massA_dec25_models` (cac, push-up,
  uniqueness; no model hypothesis left), `massA_singular_dec25_models` (existence; `hreg`, (b′)),
  `forall_exists_massA_dec25_models_iff` (existence for every `E_{≥0}`-manifold iff (b′), for the
  Lean's class of manifolds and its maximal-atlas reading of the charts, as OQ-64 does; under a
  sub-atlas reading the « only if » is not established).
* Non-vacuity: `massA_dec25_line` (`ℝ`, one model, `Sing = ∅`), `massA_dec25_minkowski`
  (`E^{1,2}` with `Isom(E^{1,2})`, one model `E^{1,2}`, `Sing = ∅`). « Natural » needs absolute
  minimality in the general DEC-25 setting: `twoLines_dec25_not_unique` (`ℝ ⊔ ℝ`, which is not an
  `E_{≥0}`-manifold, under DEC-25, a second, non-minimal causality).

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper | here |
|---|---|
| `E_{≥0}`-manifold | ⚠ reading (DEC-25): `[SingularGXStructure G X M]`, the singular points in `X_A`-charts (`hcov`), as `existsUnique_causality_singularGX_dec25`; for the models of `E_{≥0}`: `X = Minkowski 2`, the models `MassAModel`, their singular structures **abstract** (instance arguments; the `E_κ`, `E₀` ones are not built) |
| `Isom(E^{1,2})` acting by morphisms | ⚠ weakened: not used by cac, push-up, uniqueness (any `G`); carried for existence (`hG`; ⚠ reading in the packaged existence forms: `Causal.Flat.isom 2` = SO₀(1,2) ⋉ ℝ^{1,2}, while (a) also holds for O⁺(1,2) ⋉ ℝ^{1,2}) |
| « natural » | ⚠ reading: every chart an isomorphism (`IsAtlasCausalityDEC25`), unique among absolutely minimal causalities (OQ-18; necessary in the general DEC-25 setting: `twoLines_dec25_not_unique`, not an `E_{≥0}`-manifold) |
| models causally arc-connected (`rem:cac_local`, `cor:model_minimal`) | `ha`, `hb` in the abstract theorems; ✓ discharged for `E^{1,2}`, `E_κ`, `E₀` |
| models push-up (`rem:pushup`) | `hpX`, `hpY` in the abstract theorems; ✓ discharged for `E^{1,2}`, `E_κ`, `E₀` |
| "its causality is the one generated by that cover" (l.1414–1415) | ⚠ weakened: absolute minimality only |
| (b) second half, the models' regular charts isomorphisms | ⚠ weakened: not used but for existence (`hreg`, named) |
| (none) | ⚠ strengthened, existence only: (b′) `hiso` (OQ-64) |
| Baire, locally compact Hausdorff (l.1402) | ⚠ weakened: not used (OQ-10) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* **Why unmarked.** (1) `E₀`'s singular structure is `E0GX.singularGX`
  (`Causal.Port.E0GXStructure`); `E_κ`'s is `EAlphaGX.singularGX`
  (`Causal.Model.EAlphaGX`). `massA_dec25_models` holds for every choice of them; the family is
  packaged as `Causal.MassAModelsInstance.massAModelSingularGX`, and the four theorems over
  `MassAModel` are instantiated with a singular point in `Causal.Remarks.MassAModelsInstance`
  (`massA_dec25_models_e0`, `epi_witness`).
  (2) « Natural » is a reading (OQ-18). (3) The
  existence half rests on `hreg` and (b′) (OQ-64), which depend on those structures.
* **Proofs.** `cor:massA_cac` and `cor:pushup_sing` are `massA_cac` and `pushup_sing` of
  `Causal.Remarks.MassiveManifold`, applied to the isomorphic charts, indexed and lifted to a common
  universe (`isAtlasCausality_isoCharts`). Uniqueness is `eq_of_agreeOn_locally` with
  `ChartIso.agree`: two causalities for which one chart is an isomorphism agree on its source, so
  no transition map, hence none of `hG`, `hreg`, (b′), enters.
* **Charts** are read as in `Causal.GXSingularDEC25`: the maximal a.e. atlas and every
  `IsAEChart` (gx's `X_A`-charts are among them, `isAEChart_iff_isAEMorphism`). The local forms
  need one isomorphic chart at each point, so they apply to a causality natural for any covering
  sub-atlas, gx's `X_A`-atlas included.
* **Models.** `E_{≥0}` is indexed by `Option {κ // 0 < κ}`. The facts `cor:model_minimal` and
  `rem:pushup` at `κ = 0`, hypotheses in `Causal.Remarks.MassiveManifold`, are discharged here by
  `Causal.E0.causallyArcConnected` and `Causal.E0LM.e0_pushUp` (`T-ett-port-e0`).
* **Witnesses.** `massA_dec25_line`, `massA_dec25_minkowski` have `Sing = ∅`, so the `X_A`-charts are
  regular (witnesses with a singular point: `Causal.Remarks.MassAModelsInstance`);
  `twoLines_dec25_not_unique` reuses `GX_maximal_not_unique` (`Causal.GXStructure`), its second
  causality non-local (kb/0014).

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
